Author: magfrump <magfrump@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Apr 27 13:05:41 2026 -0700

    feat: redirect cache + analytics writes to /tmp on Vercel

    The LLM cache and analytics log used to write to data/ at the project
    root, which is read-only on Vercel Functions. Writes were silently
    swallowed by upstream try/catch — features just degraded with no
    indication anything was off. Switching to /tmp on Vercel keeps both
    features working within a warm container at zero new dependencies.

    Tradeoff: /tmp lifetime is the warm container, so cache benefits and
    analytics history don't survive cold starts. That's acceptable for
    single-tenant deploys — users running their own copy don't have a
    strong durability requirement, and self-hosted deploys still get the
    durable data/ path.

    Local dev is unchanged.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

